  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $6$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}6(5r-2s)-11r & = \\\\ 6\\cdot 5r+6\\cdot (-2s)-11r & = \\\\ (30r)+(-12s)-11r & = \\\\ 30r-12s-11r\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30r-12s-11r & = \\\\ (30r-11r)-12s & = \\\\ 19\\,r-12\\,s\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
